# Eternal Realms — Aethoria 2D

## Easiest way to start on Windows

Double-click **`START_AETHORIA.bat`**.

The launcher will:
1. Check for Node.js.
2. Install the game dependencies if needed.
3. Build the Vite game.
4. Start the Aethoria server and WebSocket world.
5. Open **Microsoft Edge** at `http://localhost:4173/`.

## Important

**Do not double-click `index.html` to play.** The source `index.html` is a Vite application entry point and needs an HTTP server. Opening it as `file://.../index.html` cannot start the React application correctly.

If you accidentally open `index.html` directly, Aethoria now shows an explanation instead of a blank page.

## Manual start

```bash
npm install
npm start
```

Then open:

```text
http://localhost:4173/
```

`npm start` builds the game before starting the production server.

## Shared world

The production server hosts the shared Aethoria WebSocket world at `/ws`. Invite links use `?join=XXXXXXXX`. Players connected to the same server session can see one another.

## Development

For UI development only:

```bash
npm run dev
```

AETHORIA - CHROME LAUNCHER

1. Install Node.js LTS and Google Chrome.
2. Double-click START_AETHORIA.bat.
3. The launcher installs dependencies, builds the game, starts the server, and opens Google Chrome.
4. Do NOT double-click index.html.

LOCAL ADDRESS:
http://localhost:4173/

PUBLIC SERVER / HTTPS:
The included server listens on HTTP port 4173. Do not expose that port directly to the Internet if you want a protected public game.
For a public deployment, put an HTTPS reverse proxy (for example Nginx or Caddy) in front of it, terminate TLS there, and proxy both normal HTTP traffic and WebSocket traffic (/ws) to localhost:4173.

The supplied public IP 143.244.207.157 was not reachable on TCP/443 when checked, so no claim is made that HTTPS is currently configured there.

